// Evasive PowerShell downloader and in-memory executor.
//
// Chain:
// if ($env:COMPUTERNAME -like '*CLEAN*') { return }
// $stage2 = Decode-Base64Utf16LE($joinedFragments)
// . ([scriptblock]::Create($stage2))
//
// The decoded stage repeats the pattern, hides the console using:
// kernel32.dll!GetConsoleWindow
// user32.dll!ShowWindow(hwnd, 0)
//
// The final embedded stage then:
// 1. Repeats the *CLEAN* anti-analysis check.
// 2. Creates a shield tray icon labeled Windows Security.
// 3. Downloads this carrier:
//
// hxxp://151[.]243[.]113[.]77/666ddd[.]png
//
// 4. Uses Invoke-WebRequest -UseBasicParsing -TimeoutSec 30, falling back to HttpClient.GetByteArrayAsync.
// 5. Searches the response for the custom marker:
//
// 89 43 48 49 4d 47 00
// \x89CHIMG\x00
//
// 6. Parses this container:
//
// \x89CHIMG\x00
// u32-BE blob_length
//
// CHP1
// u16-BE key_length
// key_bytes
// u32-BE encrypted_length
// XOR-encrypted gzip data
//
// 7. Decrypts the data with repeating-key XOR.
// 8. GZip-decompresses it into UTF-8 PowerShell.
// 9. Creates another ScriptBlock and executes it in memory.
// 10. Attempts to clear Run-dialog history under:
//
// HKCU:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\RunMRU

// Into Stego  
// hxxp://151[.]243[.]113[.]77/666ddd[.]png
//
// Evasive PowerShell downloader and in-memory executor.
//
// 666ddd.png is a carrier for a covert NetSupport Manager RAT deployment.
// 
// - Size: 4,799,509 bytes
// - PNG: valid 96x96 RGB image
// - SHA-256: 3341d939b43c52d0f254b3020bd396f05cd874fa1873dffad839a0d927edee87
// - Appended CHIMG container offset: 0x6CA9
// - Decoded PowerShell: 11,700,426 bytes
//
// The payload embeds 27 files. SecurityHealth.exe is a renamed NetSupport client loader: it imports _NSMClient32@8 from PCICL32.dll and contains
// NetSupport Manager Remote Control and client32.pdb strings.
// 
// Behavior:
// 
// - Deploys the bundle under %ProgramData%\<random-name> or %ProgramData%\AppDataCache.
